<title>USA: Mariner Health Q1 net increases.</title>
<headline>Mariner Health Q1 net increases.</headline>
<dateline>NEW LONDON, Conn. 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months</p>
<p>								 Ended</p>
<p>								March 31,</p>
<p>							  1997	  1996</p>
<p> Total operating revenue			174,413     135,179</p>
<p>Pre-tax income before merger costs</p>
<p>   and other nonrecurring items		12,059	 9,810</p>
<p> Merger costs and other nonrecurring items	-	 6,511</p>
<p> Pre-tax income				    12,059	 3,299</p>
<p> Provision for income taxes		   (5,306)     (1,254)</p>
<p> Net income					   6,753	 2,045</p>
<p>Per Share Data:</p>
<p> Net income					    0.23	  0.07</p>
<p> Oper shr						0.23	  0.21</p>
<p> Weighted average shares outstanding   29,173,580  29,235,065</p>
<p>Pro Forma Data:</p>
<p> Net income							   6,082</p>
<p> Net income per share						0.21</p>
<p> Weighted average shares				   29,235,065</p>
<p>(in thousands, except supplemental and per share data)</p>
<p>NOTE:  Mariner Health Group Inc said the pro forma data assumes the exclusion of merger costs and other nonrecurring items, extraordinary items and a 38% tax.</p>
<p>Operating income for the first quarter of 1997 was $6,753,000, or $0.23 per share, as compared with operating income (before merger and other non-recurring charges) of $6,082,000, or $0.21 per share, for the first quarter of 1996.</p>
